<div type="letter">
<pb facs="1362253" n="1"/>
  <opener><salute>Sir</salute></opener>
  <p><lb/>Altho I have nothing to say worth your reading, yet I beg
      <lb/>leave to send you my compliments by your <rs type="person">Coosine</rs><note type="comment" resp="SG">Als Überbringer kommt Nicolaus II Bernoulli in Betracht. Sein <rs type="letter" key="B_991170517063405501">Brief vom 14. Juni 1720</rs> belegt eine persönliche Begegnung mit Stirling während seines Aufenthalts in der Republik Venedig. Dieser Beleg setzt nicht voraus, dass beide Schreiben denselben Anlass betreffen. Die Identifizierung des Überbringers und die genaue Datierung des vorliegenden Briefes bleiben offen.</note>, who is
      <lb/>just now going to deprive us of his good Company, and indeed
      <lb/>I knew so litle time before hand of his going that I had but
      <lb/>just time <add>to</add> <del><gap/></del>write you this. There is nothing going on here
      <lb/>in the <choice><orig>Mathematical</orig><reg>mathematical</reg></choice> way, but what are things of an inferior
      <lb/>rank, and therefore rather than trouble you with trifles, I <choice><orig>shal</orig><reg>shall</reg></choice>
      <lb/>wish that your ingenious speculations may be communicated
      <lb/>to the publick<choice><orig>,</orig><reg>;</reg></choice> I am with the greatest respect</p>
  <closer><lb/>Sir
      <lb/>Your most obedient <choice><orig><g ref="#and">&amp;</g></orig><reg>and</reg></choice>
      <lb/>most humble servant
      <lb/><signed><rs key="pers_DE-588-117260266" type="person">Ja<choice><orig>:</orig><reg>.</reg></choice> Stirling</rs></signed></closer>
  <postscript>
    <p><lb/><abbr>P. S.</abbr> I hope the <rs type="letter">answere</rs> I sent
        <lb/>to you, came safe to hand,
        <lb/>and proves to your Satisfaction<choice><orig></orig><reg>.</reg></choice></p>
  </postscript>
<pb type="empty" facs="1362255" n="2"/>
</div>
</body>
